WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.060
I think one of the real great

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:03.400
lessons and good things that came

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.340
out of COVID is, I think

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.860
it I think empathy went up.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.300
You know,

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.330
a lot of leaders, a lot of people

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:15.910
in leadership positions

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:17.480
when COVID struck, they

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:18.599
picked up the phone and called their

00:00:18.599 --> 00:00:19.789
team members one by one and said,

00:00:19.789 --> 00:00:21.460
"Are you OK?"

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.460
Whether

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:23.460
they were effective or ineffective

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.460
leaders prior to COVID, they did

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:25.460
that.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:26.460
They just defaulted to

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:27.569
being human.

00:00:27.569 --> 00:00:28.730
And the irony is that's just

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:29.849
called good leadership.

00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:30.849
Like you

00:00:30.849 --> 00:00:31.849
should have been doing that.

00:00:31.849 --> 00:00:32.960
And I hope you continue to do that.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.390
It's not just in this moment of

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:35.390
time.

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:36.390
And you

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:37.390
talk about the infinite game and

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:38.910
worthy rivals and competitors,

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:39.980
there's not a single company on the

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:40.980
planet.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:41.980
When COVID struck that was

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:43.300
obsessed with beating their

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.300
competition.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.300
Every single one of them was

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.430
obsessed with just staying alive.

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:48.960
And by the way, that's an infinite

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:49.960
mindset.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:51.340
The obsession with staying in the

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:53.120
game and staying alive is this

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.160
is the correct mentality in good

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.550
times or bad times.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:59.610
And so the point is is the irony is,

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:01.080
is that those skill

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.489
set are many of them are innate.

00:01:03.489 --> 00:01:04.820
We just for some, for some reason,

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:05.820
ignore them or suppress them or

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.189
think that they're only relevant at

00:01:07.189 --> 00:01:11.880
one time and not another.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.630
And

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:15.750
I think that was, you know, when we

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:16.990
all went virtual,

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:19.270
you know, and we saw people

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:20.609
disheveled

00:01:20.609 --> 00:01:23.229
and, you know, sometimes leaders,

00:01:23.229 --> 00:01:24.890
they put on a brave face all the

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:25.890
time.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:26.890
They always have all the

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:27.890
answers.

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:28.890
They're always confident,

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:29.890
always happy, always good.

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:30.890
And that actually sometimes

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.329
backfires.

00:01:32.329 --> 00:01:34.439
I had when I was young in my career,

00:01:34.439 --> 00:01:36.280
I had my first time having a direct

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:37.569
report, had one direct report,

00:01:37.569 --> 00:01:38.569
Cynthia.

00:01:38.569 --> 00:01:39.569
She made me look good every

00:01:39.569 --> 00:01:40.569
day and it was my

00:01:40.569 --> 00:01:42.630
habit to let her sit

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:43.950
in in more senior meetings just to

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.479
learn she would have no role.

00:01:45.479 --> 00:01:46.810
I would just invite her to sit in.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.369
Why not, right?

00:01:48.369 --> 00:01:50.030
And we had a very senior client

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:52.020
call with me and a couple of

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:53.700
a bunch of the senior folks.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.141
And Cynthia was just sat on the on

00:01:55.141 --> 00:01:56.280
the sidelines to listen, and it was

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.999
a very frustrating call that did not

00:01:57.999 --> 00:01:58.999
go well.

00:01:58.999 --> 00:02:00.899
And when we hung up the the when

00:02:00.899 --> 00:02:02.999
we hung up the conference call, I

00:02:02.999 --> 00:02:04.810
vented, it all

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:06.880
came out negativity

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.630
against this client, right?

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:09.720
In front of people who were more

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.340
senior than me or peers who I

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.970
trusted and some of them were, you

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:14.940
know, mentors.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.420
And so I felt safe doing it.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:17.420
And then I turn around, I see

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:18.970
Cynthia sitting there, and as

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:19.970
we're walking out of the meeting, I

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:21.330
00:02:19:23 00:02:21:02
go, "Oh, I'm so sorry, you shouldn't

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:22.330
have seen that.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.330
That was totally

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.330
unprofessional.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.330
I totally

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:26.330
apologize."

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:27.330
And she said, "No, no,

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:28.330
no.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:29.330
I'm so glad

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:30.330
you did that because

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:31.330
I have been frustrated with this

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.330
client and I've been struggling with

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:33.330
this client.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.330
And you're always happy

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:35.330
and you're always good and you're

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:36.330
always competent.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:37.700
And I started to believe it was me.

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:39.390
And seeing your frustration made

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.950
me feel it's not me."

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:44.000
And so when we saw our leaders

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:47.080
and our on our colleagues disheveled

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.760
and tired and

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.011
and scared, it

00:02:51.011 --> 00:02:53.550
actually made us come together

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.480
when we saw their kids

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.980
run through the screen or their

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:00.540
puppy get in the way.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.100
All of a sudden, they became human.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.400
They have families.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:04.900
We knew what their houses look like.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:06.250
We knew what their design sense look

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:07.250
like.

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:08.250
I hate it when people put

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:09.250
those artificial backgrounds because

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:11.360
I actually want to see your space.

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.230
You know, how come you have no art

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:15.170
on any of your walls?

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:18.570
You know, buy that person, some art,

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:19.570
I know what I'm getting you for your

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:21.890
next bonus, you know?

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:23.350
But I thought it made us a lot more

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:24.350
human.

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:25.350
And what I'm really hoping,

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.320
I'm hoping, is that some of that

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:28.470
survives.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:30.160
That we do get to know somebody and

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:32.180
know the names of their kids

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:33.180
and know that they've got a four

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:34.180
year old sitting on their lap.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.400
Like, I thought that was beautiful,

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.170
and it made us all more more patient

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:38.170
too.

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:39.170
Like, we didn't care that

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:40.410
they were distracted for a minute,

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:40.610
you know?

